          "comment": "Useful 2yo; likely needed run on reappearance and could fare lot better now",
          "spotlight": "Strong 6f form as a 2yo, winning twice and good third in the Redcar Two-Year-Old Trophy (soft) on final start; weakened as if needing the run in strong 3yo handicap at York (6f, good to firm; Double Rush third) on reappearance five weeks ago; could leave that well behind, particularly with the yard firing on all cylinders again.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-08-29",
              "horse": "Northern Ticker",
              "horse_id": "hrs_40918962",
              "race": "Premier Electrical EBF Novice Stakes (GBB/IRE Incentive Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11359205",
              "course": "Carlisle",
              "course_id": "crs_208",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1282",
              "quote": "Northern Ticker won on the all-weather and that race has worked out well. I could have just done with a lead probably a little bit longer but at least he's had a bit of a race and learned a bit today. All his work at home's been very good. He's one of the best horses I've ridden for a long time. He's still a big baby as well and a winter on his back will do him the world of good - Paul Mulrennan, jockey."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "I've always liked him. He ran well in his first race at Carlisle behind Line Of Force. I didn't want to run him on firm ground, which is why he then went on the all-weather at Newcastle. He won very well by five lengths and we're looking at Carlisle on Thursday to give him more experience. Then, possibly if the ground is all right and he gets on okay there, the plan would be the Redcar Two-Year-Old Trophy on October 5. He looks pretty useful. 28-08-24"
            }
          ],
