          "comment": "Good Hamilton record but all 22 career starts at 5f so this trip is an unknown",
          "spotlight": "All 22 starts over 5f, winning twice in the mud here last summer; added to his tally in Carlisle Class 4 (good to soft) in May but not in the same form twice since; the return to Hamilton is a plus but his effectiveness at this trip has to be taken on trust.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-03-05",
              "horse": "Moonstone Boy",
              "horse_id": "hrs_34471850",
              "race": "Boost Your Acca With BetUK Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11184511",
              "course": "Southwell (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_10244",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1094",
              "quote": "That was very straightforward. Moonstone Boy has been knocking on the door and deserved to win. Iain [Jardine, trainer] and Andrew [Mullen, regular jockey] said to me that he'd come on leaps and bounds from his first run here. He's got a lot of speed - Paul Mulrennan, jockey, speaking on Sky Sports Racing."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He's won on the all-weather and he's also run quite well on the turf but he must have soft ground. He's plenty quick enough and is a hard-knocking sprinter whose trip is 5f. We're giving him a slightly easier time and will look for races in the next wet spell. He's back on a nice mark. 26-07-24"
            }
          ],
