          "comment": "Progressive 3yo, shaping very well at York latest; can show he's still on a good mark",
          "spotlight": "Much improved this year, winning an AW maiden in fine style on his reappearance and rewarding market support when seeing off nine rivals in a handicap at the Newmarket Craven meeting (6f, good to soft); raced away from the main action and shaped very well when third of 18 in traditionally strong 3yo handicap at York (6f, good to firm) five weeks ago; non-runner due to unsuitable ground (good to firm) at Newmarket last week; almost certainly still on a good mark.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-04-16",
              "horse": "Double Rush",
              "horse_id": "hrs_44417534",
              "race": "bet365 Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11575096",
              "course": "Newmarket",
              "course_id": "crs_988",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "I think Double Rush is going to be a nice, improving horse through the season. Some of our horses just weren't right last season and he had a nice mark. He probably didn't handle the track today and a flatter track would suit him better. There is a nice valuable handicap at York around a week before Royal Ascot which we could aim at. We will see how he improves and take it step by step. We couldn't put a hand on but the horses just weren't last right season. They looked great but just weren't letting themselves go. They seem nice and healthy this year - Charlie Hills, trainer."
            }
          ],
