          "comment": "Competitive in Listed/Group 3 events around 1m2f on last two outings",
          "spotlight": "Built upon 2yo promise with easy win in Nottingham handicap (1m2f, good) in April; improved again with Listed third at Chester (10.3f, good) and ran to a similar level when fifth (Arabian Force 2l behind in seventh) of 12 in 1m2f Royal Ascot Group 3 (good to firm) since.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He's tough, tries really hard and keeps on improving. He's probably not far off being the best horse by Ribchester - he'd certainly be in the top three anyway. He scooted up at Nottingham on his return this season and then was a really good third in the Dee Stakes at Chester from the widest draw. He proved that was no fluke when fifth at Royal Ascot last time in the Group 3 Hampton Court behind Trinity College. To be honest he absolutely hated that fast ground - I see him as a horse who would go on heavy ground, so we can mark that effort up. I think if we can find him a bit of cut in the ground we might be able to improve him a little bit more. The next target pencilled in for him is the Listed Glasgow Stakes at Hamilton on July 18 in the hope that it's the only place you'll find soft ground in July. But if the heatwave continues we'll need to have a rethink. 09-07-25"
            }
          ],
