          "comment": "Went close at Musselburgh in May but merely sixth on his two starts since",
          "spotlight": "Runner-up three times in the spring, beaten just a neck at Musselburgh (5f, good) in May, and a good case can be made on that form; however, he's finished merely sixth the last twice and his losing run is up to 12 races.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He's had a huge amount of issues but thankfully they all are behind him now. He's a very good-looking horse and I always anticipated he'd start winning races, so it wasn't a surprise to see him win last time out. He just needed his first run of the year and he got it right at Southwell. It's a lot easier to bridge a gap in sprint races than in middle-distance contests, so I think he'll run in some nice races and will continue to be competitive even up in grade. A track like Epsom would suit him very well and I could see him popping up in a nice race this season and picking up the pieces on the right day. 29-03-24"
            }
          ],
