          "comment": "Runner-up in this race two years ago but well beaten on reappearance at Newbury in May",
          "spotlight": "Lightly raced since finishing second in this two years ago when 4lb higher; he may have needed his comeback run at Newbury in May but was well beaten and needs to be an entirely different proposition two months on.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "This is a quality colt who made his debut a few days before Christmas when successful at Kempton over 1m3f. He went off at a big price [22-1] but it came as no surprise as he had been pleasing me. He's a striking individual who I didn't think would run last year, but he was going so well and I thought we might as well give him a day out, despite how late in the year it was. He did it nicely and is now rated 85. I had hoped to start him earlier this season, but he got an infection in his off-hind a couple of months ago. He's fine now and back in work. He's our big Derby hope so I need to get a prep race into him and the two options I have are either the Fairway Stakes at Newmarket or the Cocked Hat at Goodwood a little later, but the latter is not ideal as it is so close to the Derby. I really love him and he's definitely good enough to be considered for Epsom. 05-05-21"
            }
          ],
