          "comment": "Some fair efforts earlier this year but on long losing run and returns from 135-day break",
          "spotlight": "Two-time turf winner who ran some fair races earlier this year and continues to edge down the weights; however, this 7yo is seeking his first win since May 2022 and returns from a 135-day break this evening.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2022-05-11",
              "horse": "Gaassee",
              "horse_id": "hrs_26692659",
              "race": "Sky Bet Race To The Ebor Jorvik Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_10529090",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "12",
              "distance_y": "2608",
              "quote": "Gaassee wasn't as impressive as I'd hoped he'd be but he won and that was the most important thing. He was lugging a bit to his left and I don't know why. He looked a bit rusty. He's in the Hardwicke but I don't know if he's up to that yet, he will be a stakes horse in time. My record in the Ebor is appalling but he'll stay and he's progressive - William Haggas, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He was formerly with William Haggas and had a short spell with Archie Watson too before coming to me. He's always had plenty of ability and was rated as high as 103 at one stage, although he's back down to 83 now. He ran very well in a classy handicap at Kempton on his latest start in March, finishing third behind Almosh'her and Arqoob, and is now back in full work after a short break. He'll be targeted at the Old Newton Cup at Haydock on July 5. 18-06-25"
            }
          ],
