          "comment": "Won at Chelmsford in April but disappointing the last twice and has to turn things around",
          "spotlight": "Won at Chelmsford (1m2f, AW) in April but he's been disappointing the last twice (1m4f, AW/good) and needs to turn things around.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He progressed as the season went on last year culminating with victory over 1m1f in a Newmarket nursery off a mark of 82. This season he has had two runs, not troubling the judge on either occasion, and he was a bit disappointing last time out at Ascot over 1m2f, where they went no gallop which did not suit him. I am still not convinced he gets 1m2f as if you watch a replay of that race he is weakening as they approach the line. I did put him in the London Gold Cup last Saturday, but it was too dry to run him. I will give him another try over 1m2f and see, but I would not be surprised if we drop him back to a milen. The key to him is the race must be run at proper pace. 28-05-23"
            }
          ],
