          "comment": "Poor form and dropped 26lb for new yard this year; asking a lot of the first-time blinkers",
          "spotlight": "Dropped 26lb in the weights in six runs for new stable since February; perhaps the addition of blinkers will help but she's not a solid option in her current form.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2023-07-11",
              "horse": "Value Added",
              "horse_id": "hrs_32499901",
              "race": "Follow @AtTheRaces On Twitter Fillies' Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_10963966",
              "course": "Wolverhampton (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_13338",
              "distance_f": "9.5",
              "distance_y": "2084",
              "quote": "This was an opportunity we couldn't resist as we've got 20,000GBP for it being a Great British Bonus race. I'd love to aim Value Added at a fillies' handicap at Goodwood over a mile and a quarter as the race looks like it'll suit her - Richard Hughes, trainer"
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She had some respectable form on the Flat for Richard Hughes - she was rated in the 80s - and appears an ideal type for juvenile hurdling. 15-11-23"
            },
            {
              "quote": "This is the second of the two horses I train for the King and Queen and she is a lovely filly. On her sole run last year she was second at Newbury, only beaten a neck after which we put her away for the winter. She wintered nicely but I was in no hurry to get her out as she had a few issues in the spring so we gave her all the time she needed. She was meant to return at Windsor but broke out of the gate, which was very frustrating. Her comeback run was at Newbury where she ran well enough to be fifth of 13. She has come out of the race well and is likely to have her first run on the all-weather next at Wolverhampton over 1m1f. 29-06-23"
            }
          ],
